sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-017: Issue a Team Invitation — Issuance Sequence
    actor TeamLead
    participant ReactUI
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant InvitationService as Invitation<br/>Service
    participant PostgreSQL

    TeamLead->>ReactUI: Select an Open slot and candidate
    ReactUI->>ReactUI: Validate slot and candidate identifiers
    alt Client validation fails
        ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Show field errors and keep invitation draft
    else Valid draft
        ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: POST /api/teams/:teamId/invitations without eventId
        ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Verify Firebase token, MFA, active verified PART, and ownership
        alt Authentication, authorization, or body fails
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400, 401, or 403 with explicit code
            ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Show failure and preserve draft
        else Authorized owner
            ExpressAPI->>InvitationService: Issue for teamId, slotId, and inviteeId
            InvitationService->>PostgreSQL: Load team, Open slot, invitee, platform LFT, and team members
            PostgreSQL-->>InvitationService: Eligibility context
            InvitationService->>InvitationService: Require active PART, LFT on, and not on requesting team
            InvitationService->>PostgreSQL: Check Pending invitee/team and slot quotas
            PostgreSQL-->>InvitationService: Current quota conflicts
            alt Preflight eligibility or quota fails
                InvitationService-->>ExpressAPI: 403 or 409 with field-specific code
                ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: No invitation created
                ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Keep slot and candidate draft
            else Preflight passes
                InvitationService->>PostgreSQL: issue_team_invitation RPC
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Lock team with owner-mutation guard
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Recheck slot, platform LFT, and membership
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Enforce unique quotas and insert Pending with now plus 48 hours
                PostgreSQL->>PostgreSQL: Persist invitee status alert
                PostgreSQL-->>InvitationService: Invitation, expiry, team, and slot role
                InvitationService-->>ExpressAPI: Pending invitation view
                ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 201 Created
                ReactUI-->>TeamLead: Show success, expiry, and refreshed outbound status
            end
        end
    end

    Note over InvitationService,PostgreSQL: TypeScript normally checks requesting-team membership and platform LFT. A legacy event-membership fallback remains when the team-scoped lookup fails.
    Note over PostgreSQL: The current RPC still gates on the Internal Shadow Event through lock_team_for_owner_mutation and checks membership by event_id.
    Note over ReactUI,ExpressAPI: Requests require no eventId, but current response DTOs expose eventId and participant UUID fields. The direct form also asks the owner for a participant UUID.

